# Generated fresh by `expo prebuild` on every build — never committed (see
# README.md's "Building an APK" section and scripts/build-tv-apk.js).
android/
ios/

# dist/ (npm run build:tv's output) is deliberately NOT ignored: the compiled
# release APK is committed so installer/adhdisplay.iss's own [Files] glob has
# something to bundle without needing to rebuild it (a full Android build is
# slow) - see that .iss's header comment. Only ever keep the current version's
# APK there; delete the previous one before committing a new build so the
# glob can't pick up two at once.

# expo-updates code signing — see codeSigning/CODE_SIGNING.md for why only the private key (not
# the certificate) is gitignored, unlike keystore/release.keystore which is fully committed.
codeSigning/private-key.pem
